*Solution Steps Walkthrough:*

1. Express the initial wavefunction $psi(x, 0)$ as a linear combination of energy eigenstates: $psi(x, 0) = sum c_n psi_n(x)$.

2. Write the time-dependent wavefunction by appending the phase factors: $psi(x, t) = sum c_n psi_n(x) e^(-i E_n t / planck)$.

3. Compute any time-dependent expectation values by integrating the product $psi^*(x, t) Q psi(x, t)$.

4. Identify the oscillation frequency of the expectation values, which is determined by the energy difference between the contributing states: $omega = (E_m - E_n)/planck$.
